{"name":"Rachel Pink","hex":"#e8b9ae","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rachel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light tan colour, chiefly with reference to cosmetic powder. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rachel"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rachel","blocks":[{"text":"Rachel was a Hebrew Bible figure, one of the Israelite matriarchs, the favorite of Jacob's two wives, and the mother of Joseph and Benjamin, two of the twelve progenitors of the tribes of Israel. Rachel's father was Laban. Her older sister was Leah, Jacob's first wife. Her aunt Rebecca was Jacob's mother. Rachel's eldest son Joseph became a prominent figure in Israelite tradition. This pre-eminence emerges in the story of Joseph, who prepared the way in Egypt for his family's exile there."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Giacobbe_e_Rachele_-_Tanzio_da_Varallo_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Giacobbe_e_Rachele_-_Tanzio_da_Varallo_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rachel","wikidata":"Q207389"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Tissot_Jacob_and_Rachel_at_the_Well.jpg/500px-Tissot_Jacob_and_Rachel_at_the_Well.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Tissot_Jacob_and_Rachel_at_the_Well.jpg/1280px-Tissot_Jacob_and_Rachel_at_the_Well.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Tissot_Jacob_and_Rachel_at_the_Well.jpg/500px-Tissot_Jacob_and_Rachel_at_the_Well.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rachel and Jacob at the Well by James Tissot (c. 1896–1902)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATissot_Jacob_and_Rachel_at_the_Well.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo_066.jpg/500px-Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo_066.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo_066.jpg/1280px-Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo_066.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo_066.jpg/500px-Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo_066.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresco by Giovanni Battista Tiepolo of Rachel sitting on the idols (1726–1728)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiovanni_Battista_Tiepolo_066.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Rachel%27s_Tomb%2C_near_Bethlehem%2C_1891.jpg/250px-Rachel%27s_Tomb%2C_near_Bethlehem%2C_1891.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedi